{
  "run_id": "PMC12941970__problem_constrained__text_64k_b_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy is equiatomic.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy is a single-phase, likely FCC, solid solution without intentional secondary phases.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is an approximately 5 at.% Ti addition to CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding Ti to CoCrFeNi will promote formation of Ti-rich oxides or precipitates during sliding.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The sliding interface will develop fine, coherent Ti-rich oxide precipitates or a continuous oxide film.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti-rich interfacial layer will be thermally stable and self-healing during operation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperatures, a protective oxide layer formed during sliding can increase wear resistance under atmospheric conditions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Ti-containing oxide or mixed-oxide film will have low shear strength and act as a solid lubricant.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide film will reduce direct metal-to-metal contact and suppress abrasive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At lower temperatures, the Ti-modified microstructure will remain largely unaltered.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti modification will preserve low-friction behavior at lower temperatures.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to base CoCrFeNi, the Ti-modified alloy will have a lower coefficient of friction throughout approximately 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to base CoCrFeNi, the Ti-modified alloy will have a lower wear rate throughout approximately 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperatures, the self-forming oxide film will minimize adhesive wear.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti-modified alloy will maintain its mechanical characteristics at room temperature.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Base CoCrFeNi has higher elevated-temperature friction and wear because it lacks a stabilizing protective oxide layer.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed performance applies to reciprocating sliding in an oxidizing ambient atmosphere from about 25 °C to 800 °C under moderate load.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    }
